1. Use React Native Docs For Layout and Core UIYou must use the official React Native Documentation for your foundational building blocks.Layout: <View>, <ScrollView>, <SafeAreaView>Text & Data: <Text>, <FlatList>User Input: <TextInput>, <Pressable>

2. Use Expo Docs For Native Device FeaturesYou must use the official Expo Documentation when you need to access specific phone hardware or advanced system APIs.Hardware: Camera, Biometrics (FaceID/TouchID), Gyroscope, AudioSystem Services: Push Notifications, Secure Store (encrypted storage), File SystemApp Structure: File-based Routing (expo-router)

A Simple Rule of Thumb 
If you are building the visual structure of your screen, check React Native docs.
If you are connecting to phone features or configuring the app environment, check Expo docs.